   STATUS of the 1/7-spread bound  mu_{1/7}(E) >= thr_k  (8<=k<=12):
     * k<=7 branch: PROVED (pigeonhole, L2).  mu_{1/7}=1.
     * k>=8 branch: REDUCED, via the PROVED inequality mu >= EWLB_A (L7), to
       the single statement  'consecutive minimizes EWLB_A'  -- a minimization
       of the SIMPLE empty-window functional (no maxgap / three-gap combinatorics).
       That statement is VERIFIED: exhaustive over all primitive E with bounded
       spread AND a large adversarial sweep up to spread 8k (0 counterexamples),
       with margin EWLB(consec) - thr_k >= 0.07 at every k (binding k=8: 0.074).
     * The independent three-gap route (L3 net-positivity + L4 per-rational
       consecutive-maximality) PROVES the supporting structure and, with L5,
       gives a second confirmation that consecutive is the global minimizer of mu.

   RESIDUAL (the one symbolic step): a closed proof that consecutive minimizes
   EWLB_A for ALL E (unbounded spread).  EWLB_A is linear in the per-speed danger
   sets, so this is strictly simpler than minimizing mu, but a uniform symbolic
   bound (cross-window correlation is positive, so Bonferroni alone fails) is not
   yet closed.  It is exact-verified with a >=0.07 margin and 0 counterexamples.

   CONCLUSION: PARTIAL.  k<=7 PROVED.  k>=8 reduced (via the PROVED bound
   mu>=EWLB) to 'consecutive minimizes EWLB', exact-verified.  Result type: PARTIAL.
